
                                    OrgSub 0.1
                                 by Florian Lohoff



Introduction:

OrgSub should be seen as a QUICK HACK. Not more, not less. I give no guaranties what
this program does or does not do. I am running this programm on my BBS and it works
fine for me, but it must not for you. MAKE BACKUPS from all "mail:users/#?/_buser3"
files and of "sysdata:subboards3" BEFORE starting this tool.



What does OrgSub ?

A little basic on how CNet stores Subboard information:

CNET has got a file (sysdata:subboards3) where it stores all subdir data. Now if
you delete a subboard from your BBS you get a hole in this file. CNET doesn`t
reorganize this file because of one reason. All users have files in their dirs
(Mail:users/#?) which do reflect this "subboards3". The number of structure in
all files point to the same subdirectory. CNet uses this Mail:users/#?/_buser3
file, for quick looking up wheter there are subboards with new Files and/or mails
because this file keeps the last enter of the User.

Now if i want to "REALLY" reorganize "subboards3" i also have to reorganize all the
"_buser3" files. This is what i do. I first find all active subboards in "subboards3"
then reorganize "subboards3" killing all holes and resetting all pointer for
parent/child/next subboard. Then i load all "_buser3" files one by one reorganizing
them by killing the same holes.

The HD space gain calculates like this:

Subboards inactive * (Users * 64 + 488)

Example:

2008 Subboards
1240 active (768 inactive)
 140 Users
-----------
HD Space Gain = 7.245.064 Bytes


Memory gain should be:

Subboards Inactive * (488 + User Online * 64)

2008 Subboards
1240 active
   7 Users (for 7 lines)
--------
max. Memory gain = 718.848 Bytes


(I had this lots of Holes because i wrote myself a Subdir adder which ads me
 a whole bunch of subs automatically from a path like generated from
 "dir aminet4: dirs all" and i did this often but this subdir adder did not
 fill up holes. And so i got more and more holes not adding many subs from
 CNet directly)

You can get the number of holes of your subboards3 file by starting
"maintenance/repair_sub" there you see the Subboards and the number of active.


How to use:

MAKE BACKUP OF "sysdata:subboard3" AND ALL "mail:users/#?/_buser3" BEFORE DOING
ANYTHING else.

I think it would be better to Quit CNet, because otherwise there could be
damaged or incorrect "_buser3" files. The assigns "SysData:" and "Mail:" should
be set.

Then just start OrgSub without any parameters and it should do its work. If any
errors appear restore you backup files and send me a mail what happened.



